### Why this is important:
Throwable is the absolute top-level parent class in Java. By catching Throwable, you guarantee that **no matter what happens**—even if the server runs out of memory or a library is completely missing—your handleAsyncCrash method will run. This ensures the batch status safely updates to ERROR and the user gets a message, rather than waiting forever.
